                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Civil War;Bull Run 1861 is ,I think, a pretty  good game.First up got to admit didn't quite take to it .yep lovely shinny Total Wars and Ultimate Generals have  turned me sadly into a glossly lover,a bit, and this game sure aint glossly..But every salient feature from the real map is there and so are all the troops and to a latent accountant  like me heaps of data if thats your thing skip  it if it isn't.The music is wonderful,adds very much to the atmosphere of the game.The  previous mentioned map is huge you can wander off right or left flanking to your hearts content.It allows manoeuvre and that's great..No bugs,  crashes , or hangups.Certainly a wargameish feel to the controls, I like that.After half an hour you start to realise this is a pretty good game.Ok  only some very brief  bitchin' and though it irks me as an infantryman I do think the artillery seems a bit weak.In this awful war artillery was pretty darned deadly, it's  not reflected quite so in this game.. Apart from that this is an excellent game and great value for money.Recommended...",
